====================================================================================================
G127 -- THE CAP'S PHYSICAL ORIGIN: is the EFE cap the fluid's causality boundary?
====================================================================================================

PART 1 -- THE FLUID'S HEALTH (exact, from the committed chain G031/G081/G03E)
  rho(r) = A/r^2, A = sqrt(G M_b a0)/(4 pi G);  P = rho sigma^2 (isothermal,
  G081's closure);  sigma^2 = C/2, C = sqrt(G M_b a0) (the 1/r-force
  coefficient = v_flat^2);  M_ph(<r) = C r/G (linear growth, G03E).

(a) c_s^2 = sigma^2 = C/2 = sqrt(G M_b a0)/2 -- CONSTANT (isothermal identity).
    MW (M_b = 7e10, canonical): C = 2.949394e+10 m^2/s^2,  sigma^2 = C/2 = 1.474697e+10 m^2/s^2,
    c_s = 121437.1 m/s = 121.4 km/s,  v_flat = 171.7 km/s,  c_s/v_flat = 0.707107 = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.707107
    w = P/(rho c^2) = sigma^2/c^2 = 1.6408e-07  -- the isothermal phantom is a
    POSITIVE-pressure gas (w > 0), not a dark-energy-style phantom (w < -1).
    r_M(7e10) = 10.210 kpc;  r_efe(7e10, L240) computed = 6.7435 kpc (committed 6.7435, G072);  registered break 6.1 kpc at M_b = 6.5e10.

(b) THE ENERGY CONDITIONS for rho = A/r^2, P = rho sigma^2 (T = diag(rho c^2, P, P, P)):
    T-independent ratios (all constants; no r-dependence anywhere):
      NEC : rho + P/c^2        = rho (1 + w)        = rho x 1.0000001641  > 0  everywhere
      WEC : rho >= 0, NEC                          = rho x 1        >= 0  everywhere
      SEC : rho + 3 P/c^2      = rho (1 + 3 w)      = rho x 1.0000004922  > 0  everywhere
      DEC : rho - |P|/c^2      = rho (1 - w)        = rho x 0.9999998359  > 0  everywhere
    numeric spot check on r in [0.05 r_M, 2 r_efe] (5 pts): EC factor spreads = 2.22e-16, 0.00e+00, 1.11e-16  -> constant to machine precision.
  [PASS] C1 [energy conditions] the deep-regime fluid satisfies NEC/WEC/SEC/DEC at EVERY radius -- there is NO energy-condition-violation radius in the isothermal phantom (w = +sigma^2/c^2 ~ 1.6e-7 for the MW; the EOS parameter is constant   w = 1.641e-07; NEC/SEC/DEC factors 1.000000 / 1.000000 / 1.000000 (constants in r)

(c) CAUSALITY: the sound horizon vs the free-fall time:
    t_ff(r) = sqrt(r^3/G M_ph(<r)) = r/v_flat (M_ph(<r) = C r/G); c_s t_ff / r = sigma/v_flat = 1/sqrt(2) = 0.707107 EXACTLY at every r:
    in one dynamical time a sound wave crosses only 70.7% of the radius --
    the fluid is causally well connected (sub-sonic crossing, fixed margin),
    and the ratio NEVER crosses 1: there is no causality boundary radius.
  [PASS] C2 [causality] c_s t_ff/r = 1/sqrt(2) < 1 at every radius: the isothermal phantom is causal everywhere; c_s^2 = sigma^2 > 0 constant, so the c_s^2 = 0 locus does not exist   c_s t_ff/r = 0.707107 (constant); c_s = 121.4 km/s = 4.05e-04 c (MW)

(d) SELF-SUPPORT: the 'c_s^2 r vs G M_ph(<r)/r class' -- the dimensionally consistent comparison is c_s^2 vs G M_ph(<r)/r (per-unit-mass):
    sigma^2 / (G M_ph(<r)/r) = (C/2)/C = 1/2 = 0.5000000000 EXACTLY at every r (G081's eta = 1/2; the equilibrium is BALANCED at every radius
    AND MARGINAL, omega^2 = 0 exact, at every radius -- G081's critical endpoint:
    the isothermal sphere sits on its own stability boundary (Ebert-Bonnor-Antonov
    family's critical edge), so nothing in the fluid's equations picks a radius.
    M_ph(<r_efe)/M_b = sqrt(a0/g_ext) = 0.6605 (0.66 MW) -- the
    cap's phantom mass fraction equals the cap factor itself (G03E's 0.62 saturation).
  [PASS] C3 [self-support] the virial ratio eta = sigma^2 r/G M_ph(<r) = 1/2 at every radius: the fluid supplies NO radius where its own pressure-gradient support fails (the support-to-gravity ratio is a constant, never zero)   eta = 1/2 exact everywhere; M_ph(<r_efe)/M_b = sqrt(a0/g_ext) = 0.6605 (MW; registered saturation 0.62)

PART 2 -- THE CANDIDATE IDENTITIES (closed forms + the committed numbers)
(i)  c_s^2 = 0 at r_cap?  NO: c_s^2 = sigma^2 = 1.4747e+10 m^2/s^2 CONSTANT > 0
     -- the pressure-gradient support does not fail at the cap in the
     isothermal EOS (the 'share saturates the residual' reading is the CLUSTER
     over-demand locus r_sat, computed in PART 3 -- not a fluid-EOS failure).
(ii) causality boundary?  NO (PART 1c): c_s t_ff/r = 1/sqrt(2) everywhere.
(iii) G008's acausal selector + the self-support class: the isothermal member of
     the polytrope family is the ONLY acausal-safe one (n < 1 diverges at the
     edge; n > 1 misses the cluster slope); within it the virial ratio is 1/2 at
     all r -- no failure radius to coincide with r_efe.
