       the EXTERNAL field exceeds the fluid's OWN field by sqrt(g_ext/a0).
     the own-field-equals-external locus:  r_eq = C/g_ext = (a0/g_ext) r_M = 0.4362 r_M
       (= 4.45 kpc MW) -- the LINEAR H033 form is this locus,
       NOT the cap; G119's discrimination stands (linear 30% off the registered 6.1).
     at g_ext = a0 (the canonical environment reading): r_efe = r_M and the fluid's
     own field at the cap equals a0 = g_ext -- the cap sits exactly where the
     environment and the phantom's own field are equal (cluster reading).
